<task id="011" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Extract the workspace-shell from external-spa (branded portal header + tab host + pane layout + dockable left/right assistant pane + sessionStorage)</title>
    <phase>P1 Workspace-shell foundation</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:004,010</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Frontend chassis refactor of the external-spa (modifying .tsx); the shell is the base every P1/P3/P5 widget mounts on; visual + theme correctness (dark + Teams) + CIAM sessionStorage preservation are load-bearing.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified frontend build over an approved prototype + existing chassis components; Sonnet 5 @ high per CLAUDE.md §8.5.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>This is the shell base — task 012 (widget registry/workspace) and every widget task build directly on the extracted shell; concurrent shell edits would collide. Must land before its dependents.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>004,010</deps>
    <tags>frontend, refactoring</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Extend src/client/external-spa into the reusable SpaarkeAi-style WORKSPACE SHELL per design.md §12 + notes/workspace-shell-foundation.md:
    a branded portal header ("Legal Department Service Portal"), a tab host, a pane layout, and a dockable (left OR right)
    assistant pane, plus a PINNED "Quick Start" first-tab slot. Reuse the SpaarkeAi workspace chassis (Xrm-free) and the
    Spaarke.UI.Components primitives; do NOT fork the Xrm-bound LegalWorkspaceApp. Preserve the CIAM per-tab sessionStorage
    isolation (NFR-05). Build to the approved prototype (spaarke-prototype/projects/2026-08-external-access-module-host).
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer + Fluent v9 / React 18 frontend engineer. Follow ADRs strictly. Skilled at extending an existing MSAL SPA into a reusable shell chassis without regressing auth/session behavior.</role>

  <goal>
    A workspace-shell scaffold in src/client/external-spa: ShellChrome (taller branded portal header "Legal Department Service
    Portal"), a tab host (tab strip with a pinned non-closable "Quick Start" first-tab slot + closable widget tabs using the
    SpaarkeAi corner-× close control), a pane layout (header → tab strip → active-tab body), and an assistant pane docked to a
    side that can toggle LEFT or RIGHT. Widget mounting itself is task 012 — 011 delivers the empty chassis with a Quick Start
    placeholder + an assistant-pane placeholder. CIAM sessionStorage per-tab isolation is preserved; build + Teams/dark theme green.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per design.md §12(A) (Foundation = WORKSPACE SHELL, reframes FR-01/FR-02) + spec.md FR-01/FR-02 (reframed to the shell) +
      FR-06 (shell extracted from external-spa) + notes/workspace-shell-foundation.md (UX model: Quick Start pinned first tab =
      "do"/wizards; widgets = "see/manage"/data; assistant dockable left/right; corner-× close on tabs; taller intranet header;
      single-header assistant with input at bottom). The chassis is Xrm-free + reusable: adopt the SpaarkeAi WorkspacePane /
      WorkspaceTabManager / assistant-dock pattern. This task is the shell base; task 012 adds the widget registry + tabbed
      role-defaulted workspace + widget library on top. Anchor the visual direction in the approved P0 prototype.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/App.tsx (extend this SPA into the shell)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/pages/WorkspaceHomePage.tsx (current home — becomes the shell workspace host)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/components/AppHeader.tsx (extend into the branded portal ShellChrome header)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/auth/ (CIAM MSAL + sessionStorage — PRESERVE; do not switch storage)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/workspace/WorkspacePane.tsx (chassis reference — pane layout)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/workspace/WorkspaceTabManager.ts (chassis reference — tab host + tab lifecycle)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/workspace/WorkspaceTabManagerComponent.tsx (chassis reference — tab strip + corner-× close)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/ (ActionCard/ActionCardRow/WorkspaceShell/SectionPanel primitives)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkChat/SprkChat.tsx (assistant pane component — placeholder mount only in 011)</file>
      <file>spaarke-prototype/projects/2026-08-external-access-module-host/src/components/WorkspaceShell.tsx (approved prototype — visual target: ShellChrome, TabStrip, assistant dock)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ux-brief.md (locked UX north-star)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>004 (P0 prototype visual-review gate — the approved shell design this task builds to). 010 (ADR-028 A3 — the dual-plane auth rule set the shell bootstrap must honor; the shell scaffold must not regress it).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 + React 18; semantic tokens ONLY; zero hardcoded hex; correct light/dark + Teams-theme parity in the Teams host (scope: all shell chrome — header, tab strip, panes, assistant dock).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">React 18 + platform-library discipline for all UI (scope: the shell + reused shared components).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">Preserve the external-SPA per-tab sessionStorage isolation for the CIAM sign-in path (documented ADR-028 exception); do NOT switch the CIAM path to localStorage or @spaarke/auth (scope: auth bootstrap only).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT fork LegalWorkspaceApp (Xrm-bound); adopt the SpaarkeAi chassis PATTERN and reuse Spaarke.UI.Components primitives — no hand-rolled shell chrome where a shared component exists (§11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Extend src/client/external-spa in place (do not create a parallel SPA); keep the Teams host adapter + MSAL v5 NAA path intact (teams-app-r1 delivered).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-050">Any dialog opened by the shell (e.g. More Services) uses SprkModal + presets — no hand-rolled dialogs (scope: shell-level modals; the widget library modal itself is task 012).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-050-canonical-modal-shell.md</file>
