    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="SpaarkeAi workspace chassis (Xrm-free)" location="src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/workspace/WorkspacePane.tsx">Adopt the pane layout + WorkspaceTabManager tab host + corner-× close + assistant dock pattern; do NOT re-host LegalWorkspaceApp.</pattern>
      <pattern name="WorkspaceShell primitives" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/ActionCard.tsx">Reuse ActionCard/ActionCardRow for the Quick Start card slot; SprkModal for More Services.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the approved prototype WorkspaceShell/ShellChrome/TabStrip + the SpaarkeAi chassis (WorkspacePane, WorkspaceTabManager, WorkspaceTabManagerComponent) + ux-brief.md; map the shell regions to reusable components.</step>
    <step order="2">Extend AppHeader into a taller branded ShellChrome portal header ("Legal Department Service Portal") per §12(A) + ux refinement 1 (intranet/website feel, semantic tokens only).</step>
    <step order="3">Build the tab host: a tab strip with a PINNED non-closable "Quick Start" first-tab slot + closable widget-tab slots using the SpaarkeAi corner-× (circle-in-upper-corner) close control; back it with the WorkspaceTabManager pattern.</step>
    <step order="4">Assemble the pane layout: header → tab strip → active-tab body, with an assistant pane docked to a side that toggles LEFT or RIGHT (default left per the AI-maturity theory); assistant = single header + input at bottom; mount a SprkChat placeholder (no tools/wiring — that is FR-26 later).</step>
    <step order="5">Populate the Quick Start pinned tab with a placeholder (ActionCard slot + "More Services" SprkModal placeholder); widget registry + role-defaulted tabs + real widgets are task 012 — leave clean extension points.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify the CIAM MSAL + per-tab sessionStorage path is untouched (NFR-05) and the Teams host adapter / NAA path still bootstraps; do not change the dual-plane authority selection (ADR-028 A3 / task 010).</step>
    <step order="7">Run npm run build:prod (external-spa); confirm green + zero console errors; run the ui-tests below.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the external-spa (npm run build:prod — NOT npm run build)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/ (workspace-shell scaffold: ShellChrome header, tab host with pinned Quick Start slot, pane layout, dockable assistant pane)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the shell loads, when rendered, then a branded portal header reads "Legal Department Service Portal", a tab strip shows a pinned non-closable "Quick Start" first tab, and an assistant pane is docked to one side — with zero console errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the assistant dock toggle, when the user docks left then right, then the assistant pane moves to that side and the tab/body layout reflows correctly (both positions render clean).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a widget tab (placeholder), when the user activates its corner-× close control, then that tab closes while the pinned Quick Start tab has NO close control and cannot be closed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given dark mode AND the Teams theme, when toggled, then all shell chrome adapts via semantic tokens with zero hardcoded hex (ADR-021).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the CIAM sign-in path, when a user authenticates, then per-tab sessionStorage isolation is preserved (NFR-05) — the auth/storage path is unchanged from the delivered external-spa; the Teams NAA path still bootstraps.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">LegalWorkspaceApp is NOT forked/imported; the shell reuses the SpaarkeAi chassis pattern + Spaarke.UI.Components primitives (negative: no Xrm dependency introduced).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Renders"><steps><step>Load the external-spa shell (mock/dev auth)</step><step>Observe header, pinned Quick Start tab, assistant pane</step></steps><expected>no console errors; header text "Legal Department Service Portal"; pinned Quick Start first tab present</expected></test>
    <test name="Assistant dock left/right"><steps><step>Toggle assistant dock to LEFT</step><step>Toggle assistant dock to RIGHT</step></steps><expected>pane moves side; layout reflows clean in both positions</expected></test>
    <test name="Dark+Teams theme (ADR-021)"><steps><step>Toggle dark mode</step><step>Toggle the Teams theme in the Teams host</step></steps><expected>tokens adapt; zero hardcoded hex; Teams-theme parity</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    Shell BASE task — parallel-safe:false because task 012 and every widget task build on the extracted shell. This delivers the
    empty chassis (header + tab host + pane layout + dockable assistant + pinned Quick Start slot); task 012 adds the widget
    registry, role-defaulted widget tabs, the widget library, and populates Quick Start; the assistant tools are FR-26 (later,
    gated by the P5 security spike). Anchor visuals to the approved P0 prototype; further pixel refinement is deferred to the project.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt; before starting; follow the task-execute pre-execution checklist. Build with npm run build:prod.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
